{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions","id":1330483,"title":"Theory: The Hearts Hearteaters Eat Are People's Emotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-11T21:14:13-07:00","id":1330483,"title":"Theory: The Hearts Hearteaters Eat Are People's Emotions","content":"Ok,so. I've been looking at the questions thread for all the information I can find on hearteaters. And I've come up with a theory. Hearteaters are horrific in a body horror sense and horrific in a psikologikal horror sense. My theory is that They eat emotions,leaving their victims as completely emotionless people,and then they possess people's bodies or control them like puppets<br /> Do you think I might be right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T00:09:15-07:00","id":1330503,"title":"","content":"The possession or puppet control is what I think. But eating emotions would be the same as the Raksha.<br /> <br /> Anyone seen the 3rd season of Stranger Things? Watching that made me think about Heart Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T05:24:24-07:00","id":1330522,"title":"","content":"My theory is that where Lunars acquire other people's shapes, Hearteaters acquire both their shape and their mind. So when a Hearteater takes on the shape of a Duke they killed, they think and feel like that Duke (with their normal intimacies remaining somewhere at the back of their mind).<br /> <br /> Which is why they're so good at the bodysnatcher horror, because when a Hearteater uses the Duke's shape to assassinate the Duke's wife, the Duke's Intimacies will cause them to <b>behave</b> the same way as the Duke even as they plunge the knife into their uncomprehending wife's chest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T05:41:46-07:00","id":1330526,"title":"","content":"A lunar can take the shape and all the memories of their victims, and pretend to have their intimacies (or get their intimacies to get their shape) so while that's possible, it still seems too similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T06:09:14-07:00","id":1330532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1330526#post1330526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lunar can take the shape and all the memories of their victims, and pretend to have their intimacies (or get their intimacies to get their shape) so while that's possible, it still seems too similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's a fine line between pretending to have someone's intimacies and actually having them, the difference between your final words being &quot;you're not my husband!&quot; and &quot;why, I don't understand...&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also Lunars need to actually adopt the target's intimacy, whereas in this case the Hearteater can gain and lose the target's intimacies at will.<br /> <br /> Plus the devs have stated that Hearteaters, Umbrals &amp; Dream-Souled don't have quite enough depth to them to warrant a full splat each, and that Hearteaters are a foil to Lunars, so it's possible that Hearteaters have a strong similarity to Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said I'd love if they went another direction entirely, I'm just not sure how to do it without Hearteaters becoming Raksha lite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-12-2019, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T06:57:00-07:00","id":1330537,"title":"","content":"Raksha eat emotions and leave their victims emotionless.<br /> Lunars copy people's forms. Often but not always by killing them.<br /> <br /> I think possession or puppeteering, without either taking people's emotions or copying them as a seperate person, would make them very different.<br /> <br /> For example, if the Hearteater eats someone's insides and then wears their body as a suit, it'd be similar to a Lunar. But if they eat their brain and then put a parasite inside so they can puppeteer their corpse at a distance, or if they psychically suck out people's will to resist and then mind-control them, with the original mind being trapped and terrified inside, then that's not really so similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T07:09:59-07:00","id":1330539,"title":"","content":"Puppeteering does sound like a good avenue and could make an interesting exalt. Plus bodysnatcher horror does involve multiple people turning on you in some cases, which would be possible if you can control multiple victims at a time.<br /> <br /> I think the only reason I'm skeptical about it is because the name Hearteater doesn't really conjure the image of a puppetmaster in my mind, which is admitedly entirely subjective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T08:29:19-07:00","id":1330551,"title":"","content":"Vance's cited bodysnatcher-style horror as the inspiration for the Hearteaters, with the best movie inspiration being Twin Peaks: Fire Walk With Me. They don't replace people like Lunars or turn them into emotionless husks like raksha; what they do is very much about the spiritual/mental.<br /> <br /> We don't know quite why they have their name, only that it's a metaphorical thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T13:49:49-07:00","id":1331107,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking the Exaltation itself is parasitic, like, it has a distinct personality and jumps between hosts. Like a worse version of what uneducated Realm-folk believe &quot;Anathema&quot; are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T14:53:48-07:00","id":1331120,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T18:07:24-07:00","id":1331142,"title":"","content":"Pardon the utter ignorance of someone who has been away of the forums for a few weeks, but where can bits of info and devs' commentary/thoughts on those so-called Hearteaters be found?<br /> <br /> This particular topic has quite sparked my curiosity on the latest developments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-15-2019, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T18:31:55-07:00","id":1331144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331142#post1331142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon the utter ignorance of someone who has been away of the forums for a few weeks, but where can bits of info and devs' commentary/thoughts on those so-called Hearteaters be found?<br /> <br /> This particular topic has quite sparked my curiosity on the latest developments.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the top of my head<br /> They were created by an Incarna in the Divine revolution.<br /> They weren't always the Heartearters,the war changed them<br /> The inspiration for them is Body Snatchers and Firewalk with me<br /> They are horrific<br /> It's even harder to play an noble hearteater than an noble Abyssal or Infernal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T19:12:05-07:00","id":1331149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331142#post1331142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon the utter ignorance of someone who has been away of the forums for a few weeks, but where can bits of info and devs' commentary/thoughts on those so-called Hearteaters be found?<br /> <br /> This particular topic has quite sparked my curiosity on the latest developments.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for where... Mostly tidbits gleamed from the Q&amp;A thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-15T23:58:16-07:00","id":1331178,"title":"","content":"They're set to get an outline in <i>Exigents</i> for fans to homebrew their own, along with the Umbral Exalted and the Dream-Souled.<br /> <br /> The lady with the aurora on the splash page on pp.54-55 of the Ex3 core is a Hearteater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T06:45:21-07:00","id":1331330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331149#post1331149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for where... Mostly tidbits gleamed from the Q&amp;A thread</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is there any compilation of such tidbits perhaps?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331178#post1331178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're set to get an outline in <i>Exigents</i> for fans to homebrew their own, along with the Umbral Exalted and the Dream-Souled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any guesstimates of when might that book eventually come out?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331178#post1331178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lady with the aurora on the splash page on pp.54-55 of the Ex3 core is a Hearteater.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, the lady that kind of reminds me of Manosque Cyan (at least in her demure Nellens dame persona), nice to know. Just one tells us about us much about the whole of them as a random pic of a Twilight or Full Moon would tell of Solars or Lunars as a whole, but that's never going to stop our wild mass guessing/preemptive homebrewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-17-2019, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-17T06:50:57-07:00","id":1331331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331330#post1331330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any guesstimates of when might that book eventually come out?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragonblood kickstarter was Spring 2018, the Lunar kickstarter was Spring 2019, so I expect the Exigents kickstarter, with text (just a few pics) to come out in Spring 2020. Then the actual book, with properly edited pictures, will be out like a year or so later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm, nice to know. Just one tells us about us much about the whole of them as a random pic of a Twilight or Full Moon would tell of Solars or Lunars as a whole, but it's better than nothing. </div> </div> </div>As Hearteaters have no castes, it might tell us marginally more, but... yeah, it doesn't really tell you much. I think the Umbral and Alchemical pictures are the most useful, the others don't tell you much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T05:29:31-07:00","id":1331575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331331#post1331331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragonblood kickstarter was Spring 2018, the Lunar kickstarter was Spring 2019, so I expect the Exigents kickstarter, with text (just a few pics) to come out in Spring 2020. Then the actual book, with properly edited pictures, will be out like a year or so later.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does make for a decent framework for reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331331#post1331331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Hearteaters have no castes, it might tell us marginally more, but... yeah, it doesn't really tell you much.</div> </div> </div> </div>What in itself makes for a good extra tidbit of info, as i remember no exalts with subdivisions, implying that while simulated with the such mechanics they might be nothing of the sort. Or maybe just an unexpected colateral from being even rarer than Infernals in 2e. Where does it come up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-19-2019, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T06:37:29-07:00","id":1331585,"title":"","content":"From what I remember of the tidbids the devs shared here and there :<br /> <br /> Their Exaltations have been twisted and their Castes are lost - they used to have Castes but they don't anymore. Their celestial creator is also dead, and would be horrified at what the Hearteaters have become if they were still alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T06:40:51-07:00","id":1331587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331575#post1331575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What in itself makes for a good extra tidbit of info, as i remember no exalts with subdivisions, implying that while simulated with the such mechanics they might be nothing of the sort. Or maybe just an unexpected colateral from being even rarer than Infernals in 2e. Where does it come up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm not quite following you here? Do you mean how did I know they had no Castes?<br /> <br /> Vance said on the Ask the Devs thread that Hearteaters, Umbrals and Dream-Souled have no Castes. Basically, because while they were cool ideas for Exalt types, there wasn't really enough to them to split into 4-5 groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T07:28:13-07:00","id":1331593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331330#post1331330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any compilation of such tidbits perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Compiled from the Ask the Devs threads:<br /> <br /> Out of universe, the Hearteaters were originally planned as thematic foils to the Lunars, alongside the Umbrals.<br /> <br /> They're not corrupted versions of any of the established Exalted types; they're a corrupted version of one particular type that no longer exists. The degree of transformation is around, or beyond, that of the Solar-Abyssal transformation.<br /> <br /> They had another name in their original version, of the &quot;(Adjective) Exalted&quot; type, but not any more. Said Exalted had an affinity for adamant (indeed, they were the missing adamant-affinity Exalted), which the Hearteaters retain.<br /> <br /> We'll get a brief discussion of what they used to be in <i>Exigents</i>, although their current themes aren't all that similar to their original versions.<br /> <br /> They were originally created by a deceased Celestial Incarna, who died before their corruption, but said death was not the direct cause of their corruption. Were their Incarna to see what's become of them, they would be horrified.<br /> <br /> They were initially created to fight in the Divine Revolution, but the war turned them into what they are now. They feel betrayed by the other Exalted they fought alongside. Someone who lived through the Divine Revolution, or had memories of it, would have a good chance of knowing what happened to them.<br /> <br /> While they don't have Castes, or Caste Marks, they will have distinctive supernatural aesthetics.<br /> <br /> They're not immediately recognizable as Anathema, but once someone figures out what a Hearteater's doing, they'll realize it's horrifying and monstrous, and needs to be shut down *fast*.<br /> <br /> Power level-wise, they're Celestial Exalted, roughly comparable to Lunars and Sids, but it's a difficult comparison to make due to them being weird. The powers themselves are very much about the spiritual/mental.<br /> <br /> They're antagonistic to most people &amp; PCs. A noble Hearteater is playing against type, trickier than Abyssals or Infernals, with obstacles those Exalted don't face, but it is possible. They probably won't fit into a mixed circle, but again it is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T08:07:48-07:00","id":1331600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331593#post1331593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Compiled from the Ask the Devs threads:<br /> <br /> Out of universe, the Hearteaters were originally planned as thematic foils to the Lunars, alongside the Umbrals.<br /> <br /> They're not corrupted versions of any of the established Exalted types; they're a corrupted version of one particular type that no longer exists. The degree of transformation is around, or beyond, that of the Solar-Abyssal transformation.<br /> <br /> They had another name in their original version, of the &amp;quot;(Adjective) Exalted&amp;quot; type, but not any more. Said Exalted had an affinity for adamant (indeed, they were the missing adamant-affinity Exalted), which the Hearteaters retain.<br /> <br /> We'll get a brief discussion of what they used to be in <i>Exigents</i>, although their current themes aren't all that similar to their original versions.<br /> <br /> They were originally created by a deceased Celestial Incarna, who died before their corruption, but said death was not the direct cause of their corruption. Were their Incarna to see what's become of them, they would be horrified.<br /> <br /> They were initially created to fight in the Divine Revolution, but the war turned them into what they are now. They feel betrayed by the other Exalted they fought alongside. Someone who lived through the Divine Revolution, or had memories of it, would have a good chance of knowing what happened to them.<br /> <br /> While they don't have Castes, or Caste Marks, they will have distinctive supernatural aesthetics.<br /> <br /> They're not immediately recognizable as Anathema, but once someone figures out what a Hearteater's doing, they'll realize it's horrifying and monstrous, and needs to be shut down *fast*.<br /> <br /> Power level-wise, they're Celestial Exalted, roughly comparable to Lunars and Sids, but it's a difficult comparison to make due to them being weird. The powers themselves are very much about the spiritual/mental.<br /> <br /> They're antagonistic to most people &amp; PCs. A noble Hearteater is playing against type, trickier than Abyssals or Infernals, with obstacles those Exalted don't face, but it is possible. They probably won't fit into a mixed circle, but again it is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanl you marin!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T18:17:10-07:00","id":1331682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331587#post1331587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I'm not quite following you here? Do you mean how did I know they had no Castes?<br /> <br /> Vance said on the Ask the Devs thread that Hearteaters, Umbrals and Dream-Souled have no Castes. Basically, because while they were cool ideas for Exalt types, there wasn't really enough to them to split into 4-5 groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, sorry for the obtuseness. What i meant to say is that the fact the Hearteaters lack castes is in itself interesting new (at least for me) information, in that it might, among other things, make one question if they are &quot;true&quot; exalts or something else altogether that &quot;just&quot; happen to use a similar set of mechanics in the table.<br /> <br /> <i>Now </i>i know that the &quot;castelessness&quot; is not a Hearteater only thing, but applies to Umbrals and Dream-Souled too - not to mention the out of universe reason that making a bunch of castes for either felt like too much work for what little there is on them. Also, the bits from the Ask the Devs topic throw my &quot;maybe not creations of the Incarnae&quot; wild guess about Hearteaters into the Abyss. Not that it is a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T20:37:42-07:00","id":1331705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331682#post1331682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it might, among other things, make one question if they are &quot;true&quot; exalts or something else altogether that &quot;just&quot; happen to use a similar set of mechanics in the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casteless Lunars are Exalted. So, too, are Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-19-2019, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T22:02:50-07:00","id":1331714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331705#post1331705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Casteless Lunars are Exalted. So, too, are Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Castelessness is a condition, a state of flux that is possible for Lunars but (afaik having not delved into 3e's take on Lunars) never the norm - and one that bring with it the potential risk of chimerization and is at least somewhat frowned upon by the many-faced heroes themselves.<br /> <br /> Exigents are a special case in all too many levels. exalts for a reason, eh?<br /> <br /> More importantly, i said <i>&quot;true&quot; </i>exalts for a reason, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T23:20:45-07:00","id":1331725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331714#post1331714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Castelessness is a condition, a state of flux that is possible for Lunars but (afaik having not delved into 3e's take on Lunars) never the norm - and one that bring with it the potential risk of chimerization and is at least somewhat frowned upon by the many-faced heroes themselves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not in 3rd ed. I mean, for most it is a temporary condition, but there's no risk of mutation and madness just from being Casteless. Of course, if you hang out in the Wyld without magic protective tattoos that risks mutation and madness, but no more than for Dragonblood, Solars, mortals, etc.<br /> <br /> Most do end up getting the tats because they're useful to protect you from wyld mutation, petrifying curses, that spell that turns your blood to magma, etc, and to get a Caste because Castes are useful.<br /> But you can stay Casteless forever if you want.<br /> <br /> Also, in the Primordial War, Lunars may have all been Casteless; it's unclear. Certainly they didn't have the five Castes they had in the High First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T00:00:12-07:00","id":1331731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331682#post1331682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Now </i>i know that the &quot;castelessness&quot; is not a Hearteater only thing, but applies to Umbrals and Dream-Souled too - not to mention the out of universe reason that making a bunch of castes for either felt like too much work for what little there is on them. Also, the bits from the Ask the Devs topic throw my &quot;maybe not creations of the Incarnae&quot; wild guess about Hearteaters into the Abyss. Not that it is a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, while the Umbrals were also created by an Incarna, the Dream-Souled are <i>not</i> - they're created by something of the Wyld, something that shares that numinous nature of the Incarnae/Dragons/Primordials that allows them to create Exalted.<br /> <br /> As best we can tell, it's not something previously known from the Wyld - ie, not raksha or Primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T05:21:52-07:00","id":1331756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331725#post1331725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in 3rd ed. I mean, for most it is a temporary condition, but there's no risk of mutation and madness just from being Casteless. Of course, if you hang out in the Wyld without magic protective tattoos that risks mutation and madness, but no more than for Dragonblood, Solars, mortals, etc.<br /> <br /> Most do end up getting the tats because they're useful to protect you from wyld mutation, petrifying curses, that spell that turns your blood to magma, etc, and to get a Caste because Castes are useful.<br /> But you can stay Casteless forever if you want.<br /> <br /> Also, in the Primordial War, Lunars may have all been Casteless; it's unclear. Certainly they didn't have the five Castes they had in the High First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is an interesting new take of things in their lore. Looks like i have to update myself on the fluff at least a little - and that is nice actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331731#post1331731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On that note, while the Umbrals were also created by an Incarna, the Dream-Souled are <i>not</i> - they're created by something of the Wyld, something that shares that numinous nature of the Incarnae/Dragons/Primordials that allows them to create Exalted.<br /> <br /> As best we can tell, it's not something previously known from the Wyld - ie, not raksha or Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that means at least two fallen Incarna and some mystery being in the Deep Wyld or beyond that felt like playing at being one, at least in a way, by making its own chosen. Curiouser and curiouser....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:18:24-07:00","id":1331825,"title":"","content":"Theory : the Hearteaters were Empath Exalted, able to connect to the mind/soul/emotions/lifeforce of others in a way that empowers both themselves and the person they are connected to. After their creator gave their life for the Exalted Host, the Hearteaters were left in a state where they are forced to use their power to feed on the mind/soul/emotions/lifeforce of other people in order to survive. Seeing this as an abomination, the Exalted Host turned on Hearteaters, creating a deep sense of betrayal since it was the Hearteaters' willingness to help the Host that led to their sorry state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:55:04-07:00","id":1331837,"title":"","content":"I can see it as something like that actually. I was certainly thinking that the original Hearteaters probably had some kind of mental or spiritual powers.<br /> <br /> Can anyone remember the themes of Adamant in 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T13:50:34-07:00","id":1331852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Adamant is like jade, but flensed of its elemental associations. It represents solidity, permanance, function. It was a favored material of the Great Maker,&quot; he paused, tapping his chin. &quot;Were there to be another Exalt type, such as it would reflect him, its material would be adamant.&quot;</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> -The Magnus (from late 2e developer interviews)<br /> <br /> Obviously, the &quot;adamant is Autocthon-associated&quot; is probably going away </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T14:09:14-07:00","id":1331856,"title":"","content":"&quot;Like Jade, but without elemental associations&quot; is pretty dull. Maybe they'll give it new themes.<br /> <br /> I'll go check Alchemicals 2nd ed, maybe that has something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T14:15:46-07:00","id":1331859,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... not terribly helpful actually, but if we're talking about mental abilities, it might be notable that while Adamant is mostly just about being really sharp, it can do stuff related to memory; Adamant Exalted in 2nd ed had the anima power of wiping people's memories of the last scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T05:46:16-07:00","id":1331942,"title":"","content":"Considering the sobriquet &quot;hearteaters&quot;, powers with a focus on the spiritual/mental and the body-snatching theme, i'm going to risk saying messing with Intimacies - stealing, implanting or getting special benefits out of them - might be part of their gimmick.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Inhabitings&quot; and &quot;Tantra&quot; set of spirit charms in RoGD and some of the Raksha charm shenanigans might offer some inspirations on what one could play with - or might want to deviate from, instead - in developing the Hearteaters own peculiar charmset.<br /> <br /> About Adamant, it might be said to be crystaline/glassy, so i would guess one could play with themes &amp; imagery related to transparency, hiding in plain sight, refraction that may cause dispersion or focus, a degree of reflectiveness through positioning, i guess.<br /> <br /> It was a direction i toyed with a few years ago, when making a group of exalts connected to a fallen Incarna of Adamant once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-21-2019, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T06:01:21-07:00","id":1331943,"title":"","content":"I think they said 2 of the 3 (Hearteaters, Umbrals, Dream-Souled) are connected with Adamant. So whatever Adamant does should be thematically linked to either Umbrals or Dream-Souled as well.<br /> <br /> Since Dream-Souled are Exalted from something in the Wyld, I'd bet against them being linked to a specific material, leaving Umbrals as the other Adamant Exalted. Umbrals being all about fighting (or giving in to) one's inner demons, the common theme with Hearteaters could be mental/social/psyche effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-21-2019, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T06:11:02-07:00","id":1331947,"title":"","content":"Did they say that? I thought it was just Hearteaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T06:18:12-07:00","id":1331948,"title":"","content":"Just looked it up, I got it wrong, they said that Hearteaters wouldn't be the only thing linked to Adamant, but all they said about it was that 1 of the 4 Exigents write-ups was resonant with Adamant. So there's no indication whether or not Dream-Souled and Umbrals are linked with Adamant.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1300597#post1300597\">Hearteaters not only thing with Adamant</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1319727#post1319727\">1 of the 4 Exigents is resonant with Adamant</a><br /> <br /> Did they say what all 4 Exigent write-ups would be? I remember Janest and Architects, but not the other 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-21-2019, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T10:04:23-07:00","id":1331976,"title":"","content":"IIRC, it's an exigent where the god either stole or got the exigence on the black market, and a freaky exigent made from different gods, described (but not in the book) as a &quot;dirty bomb&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which doesn't actually tell you the themes or power level of either of them. Though I'm going to guess the black market exigent is not exalted by the god of honesty and fighting corruption.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T12:08:30-07:00","id":1331998,"title":"","content":"We're not using the &quot;dirty bomb&quot; nomenclature going forward. It's anachronistic, and its connotations aren't necessarily an ideal fit for how we expect to handle them in <i>Exigents</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T12:10:27-07:00","id":1332000,"title":"","content":"That seems sensible; what I thought of when I heard &quot;dirty bomb&quot; didn't really fit the details given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T03:05:41-07:00","id":1333081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331852#post1331852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The Magnus (from late 2e developer interviews)<br /> <br /> Obviously, the &amp;quot;adamant is Autocthon-associated&amp;quot; is probably going away [/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is it obvious this is a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T03:11:30-07:00","id":1333082,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's obvious, but I see no reason it should be the case either. Clearly Hearteaters are not to do with Autochthon; their incarna was someone else.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... did they say Umbrals were also made by an Incarnae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T07:42:11-07:00","id":1333253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1333082#post1333082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... did they say Umbrals were also made by an Incarnae?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I did!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T07:52:35-07:00","id":1333256,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> Okay, so the Incarnae are the gods of...<br /> The sun<br /> The moon<br /> The 5 planets<br /> Something else<br /> Something else possibly connected to darkness<br /> <br /> I wonder if the Umbral incarnae was/is god of the night sky or something.<br /> <br /> (Anyone remember what's been said about the Umbral incarnae? Are they still alive?)<br /> <br /> So what could the Hearteaters' Incarnae have been god(dess) of? I guess there the thing us it might be something in the sky that no longer exists, like another moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T09:38:10-07:00","id":1333269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1333256#post1333256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> Okay, so the Incarnae are the gods of...<br /> The sun<br /> The moon<br /> The 5 planets<br /> Something else<br /> Something else possibly connected to darkness<br /> <br /> I wonder if the Umbral incarnae was/is god of the night sky or something.<br /> <br /> (Anyone remember what's been said about the Umbral incarnae? Are they still alive?)<br /> <br /> So what could the Hearteaters' Incarnae have been god(dess) of? I guess there the thing us it might be something in the sky that no longer exists, like another moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it was Uranus on the sly who done it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12796-beast-of-bitter-oblivion","name":"Beast of Bitter Oblivion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T12:42:55-07:00","id":1333290,"title":"","content":"More planets is certainly feasible, though might feel a bit odd when exalts of Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter and Saturn are really, really similar and this other one is not; but it shouldn't be hard to write an explanation (those 5 worked together, but their sister Uranus made hers by herself, or something).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T17:47:37-07:00","id":1333329,"title":"","content":"Auroras and other sky-based phenomena would be my guess, rather than planets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T01:28:14-07:00","id":1333361,"title":"","content":"I think it's been mentioned that the Aurora Borealis exists in Creation, so that could work.<br /> <br /> Probably not for Umbral Exalted though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T05:29:20-07:00","id":1333378,"title":"","content":"For Umbral, maybe the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belt_of_Venus\" target=\"_blank\">Belt of Venus</a>? It's about the only atmospheric phenomenon I see that causes a &quot;dark&quot; effect. Plus the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belt_of_Venus#/media/File:Moon_and_red_blue_haze.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">colors</a> somewhat match the Umbral character's color theme and the sky behind him as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T14:56:58-07:00","id":1334026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1333361#post1333361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's been mentioned that the Aurora Borealis exists in Creation, so that could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this time of year? At this time of day? In this part of Creation? Localized entirely within your patron?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T16:10:17-07:00","id":1334033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1334026#post1334026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this time of year? At this time of day? In this part of Creation? Localized entirely within your patron?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And no, you can't see it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T18:38:54-07:00","id":1342445,"title":"","content":"Our Sidereals game is coming to the end of a story about a Hearteater preying on the poor of Cherak.<br /> <br /> It felt really creepy and claustrophobic at times due to this sense that when we were walking through the street at night he always had a pair of eyes on us and as we near the home stretch our Endings fought an Immaculate Monk we had befriended who had become entralled and was struggling for control of his own body. I don't know if they're going to be like that in Exigents but this has made for an interesting enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T18:41:55-07:00","id":1342446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1342445#post1342445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our Sidereals game is coming to the end of a story about a Hearteater preying on the poor of Cherak.<br /> <br /> It felt really creepy and claustrophobic at times due to this sense that when we were walking through the street at night he always had a pair of eyes on us and as we near the home stretch our Endings fought an Immaculate Monk we had befriended who had become entralled and was struggling for control of his own body. I don't know if they're going to be like that in Exigents but this has made for an interesting enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those guys sound scary!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T23:12:55-07:00","id":1342478,"title":"","content":"All signs very clearly point to \u201cKill-and-replace and/or possess people for the purpose of doing horror villain things.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1331107#post1331107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking the Exaltation itself is parasitic, like, it has a distinct personality and jumps between hosts. Like a worse version of what uneducated Realm-folk believe &amp;quot;Anathema&amp;quot; are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Denied on Discord a while back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T19:50:07-07:00","id":1343912,"title":"","content":"Our Hearteater story ended with more than a note of tragedy as the defeated Exalt turned out to be in a similar struggle for control with his former incarnation. A struggling musician who just wanted an audiance contending with the more malevolent urges of the previous incarnation who wanted to avenge themselves on Cherak. In the end we gave him an audiance for his final performance before our Endings freed him from the struggle, sending his soul to Lethe and freeing his thralls in the process.<br /> <br /> Of course it wasn't all good news. He explained before his last performance that one of the thralls will inherit the Exaltation, but maybe the fact he was choosing to go out on a high note will make things easier for the next person.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T20:01:23-07:00","id":1343914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1343912#post1343912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our Hearteater story ended with more than a note of tragedy as the defeated Exalt turned out to be in a similar struggle for control with his former incarnation. A struggling musician who just wanted an audiance contending with the more malevolent urges of the previous incarnation who wanted to avenge themselves on Cherak. In the end we gave him an audiance for his final performance before our Endings freed him from the struggle, sending his soul to Lethe and freeing his thralls in the process.<br /> <br /> Of course it wasn't all good news. He explained before his last performance that one of the thralls will inherit the Exaltation, but maybe the fact he was choosing to go out on a high note will make things easier for the next person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating. Did yu homebrew it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T20:10:51-07:00","id":1343917,"title":"","content":"Yup. It's a 3rd edition Sidereals game so we're already pretty homebrew dependent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T20:21:37-07:00","id":1343918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330483-theory-the-hearts-hearteaters-eat-are-people-s-emotions?p=1343917#post1343917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. It's a 3rd edition Sidereals game so we're already pretty homebrew dependent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}